+# FINDINGS
+
+## Summary
+
+I would not sign off on this vault for Monday mainnet deposits.
+
+The existing 39 tests still pass, but they miss the deployment-critical paths:
+
+- the vault cannot complete a first deposit against real mainnet USDT and the real Aave V3 pool;
+- the vault accounts for an internal principal counter instead of the live aUSDT balance, so Aave yield is not reflected in shares;
+- withdrawal fees can become permanently unowned aUSDT when the final shareholder exits.
+
+I added only `test/UsdtYieldVaultFailureEvidence.t.sol`. I did not modify `src/`, `test/UsdtYieldVault.t.sol`, or `test/mocks/`.
+
+## Finding 1: mainnet USDT/Aave deposit reverts
+
+### Impact
+
+The vault is configured to use mainnet USDT at `0xdAC17F958D2ee523a2206206994597C13D831ec7` and Aave V3 Pool at `0x87870Bca3F3fD6335C3F4ce8392D69350B4fA4E2`. On a mainnet fork, a user approval and `transferFrom` into the vault succeed, and the vault's direct `usdt.approve(address(aavePool), amount)` call reaches real USDT. Real USDT returns no boolean value from `approve`; the high-level `IERC20.approve` call in `deposit` reverts before Aave `supply` is called.
+
+This makes the vault unusable with the intended underlying.
+
+### How I found it
+
+I forked mainnet at block `26_026_344`, deployed the vault against the exact addresses from `README.md`, dealt USDT to a test depositor, approved the vault using a low-level call compatible with legacy USDT, and called `deposit`.
+
